From 2c2e2fe79ba1f7d31eba31d8f3ac26e6bd265cd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 07:33:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Add the solitaire gameplay layer

The Solitaire assembly was an empty asmdef, so GameFlow charged the entry
cost, found no ILevelRunner in the level scene, refunded and logged an
error. This fills it in with a playable tri-peaks round.

- Card/CardDeck: the deck and the matching rule (one rank apart, wrapping
  between Ace and King), with a seeded shuffle so a level deals the same
  board every attempt.
- SolitaireBoardLayout: slot positions and coverage in card widths, not
  pixels. Empty means the classic three peaks over ten free cards.
- SolitaireGame: the rules, the combo scoring and the win/lose decision,
  with no Unity types in the way, so it is testable outside play mode.
- SolitaireLevelRunner: implements ILevelRunner, builds the board from the
  level's rule asset and reports exactly one LevelResult. It never touches
  the wallet - GameFlow still owns the money.
- Placeholder card art built from UI primitives, to be replaced by prefabs
  once the real art lands.
- Assets/Scenes/Solitaire.unity: the scene GameFlow loads by name, with its
  own EventSystem because the hub's is switched off while a level runs.
- 13 edit-mode tests covering the deal, blocking, matching, scoring, the
  win and lose transitions and the seeded deal.

Level 1 keeps its authored economy and now points at the new rules asset,
so playing it deals a classic tri-peaks board.
