From 4d597c56407ffb43cc54c2a3c23699db82a10fc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 07:35:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Add the object progress window views

Scripts behind the scene progress popup, so the window built in Hub 1 has
something driving it.

- ObjectProgressWindow: spawns one Bar per object in the chapter into the
  scroll view's Content, and refreshes them when a purchase lands or a
  balance moves. It owns the subscriptions so the rows do not - a chapter
  with fifty objects still has one listener. Open/Close/Toggle are public
  for the progress and close buttons.
- HubObjectBarView: one row. Icon, name and either a price or an owned
  badge; the button calls ProgressionService.TryPurchase and goes quiet
  when the object is bought or the player cannot pay.
- HubObjectDef gains an Icon for the list portrait, falling back to the
  world sprite while there is no art.

The headline and the progress bar at the top of the window are not
duplicated here: ChapterProgressView already renders the chapter name, the
x/y and the fill, so it goes on the window's bar as it does on the hub's.
