From 1b2ea896b45ab14377ff20f2b51f9647776fdcf9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 07:41:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Add the chapter completion reward

The chest at the end of the progress bar had nothing behind it: the chapter
carried no reward and ChapterCompleted fired with nobody listening.

- HubChapterDef gains CompletionRewards, paid out through the wallet like
  any other grant.
- ProgressionService.TryClaimChapterReward pays it once. Nothing claims it
  automatically - the player taps the chest, so the moment can be given a
  celebration later.
- PlayerProfile remembers claims by chapter id, so renaming an asset cannot
  hand the chest out a second time. Older saves simply have none claimed.
- GameBootstrap saves on ChapterRewardClaimed too: a chapter whose reward
  is empty moves no money, and would otherwise leave the claim unsaved.
- ChapterProgressView takes an optional chest button, interactable only
  while the reward is unclaimed and the chapter is done.

Three tests cover it: no claim before the chapter is finished, a claim that
pays and reaches the profile, and a second claim that pays nothing.
